        "z": "f353021935d92ed7",
        "name": "Databased Function",
        "func": "// 1. Add a timestamp to the incoming sensor data so you know when it arrived\nmsg.payload.timestamp = new Date().toISOString();\n\n// 2. Generate today's date for the filename (Format: YYYY-MM-DD)\nlet dateString = new Date().toISOString().split('T')[0];\n\n// 3. Set the dynamic file path/name\n// Note: Make sure the folder \"C:/iot_logs/\" actually exists on your computer!\nmsg.filename = \"G:\\\\iot_logs\\\\energy_data.json\";\n\n// 4. Convert the data object into a JSON text string so the file can read it\nmsg.payload = JSON.stringify(msg.payload);\n\n// 5. Send the message forward to the write file node\nreturn msg;",
